# API & services

## Client
- Call backend only through `httpClient` / helpers in `src/lib/client.ts`
- Pass Sanctum Bearer via `token` argument when the route needs auth
- POST flows may need Sanctum CSRF (`/sanctum/csrf-cookie`) — keep existing client behavior
- On 401 with a Bearer token, session sign-out is handled in the client — do not hard-redirect alone

## Service files
- One domain per file under `src/services/` (e.g. `order.service.ts`)
- Export async functions; keep routes as path strings relative to `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export const getProduct = async (slug: string, token?: string | null) => {
  return httpClient({ route: `/product/${slug}`, token });
};
```

## Important endpoints
- Homepage: `/homepage/*`
- Order: `GET /product/{slug}`, `POST /promo/check`, `POST /transaction/store`
- Invoice: `GET /transaction/invoice/{invoice}` (poll ~10s when status `0`)
- Track: `GET /transaction/latest?q=`
- Auth: `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/register`
- Account: `/dashboard/*`, `/balance`, `/auth/user`, `/api-keys`

## Transaction status
`0` menunggu bayar · `1` lunas · `2` diproses · `21` pending · `3` berhasil · `100` gagal

## Store payload shape
`product_id`, `price_id`, `price_type`, `user_information` (JSON string), `whatsapp`, `email`, `payment_method`, optional `code`, `quantity`
